-## Optimizations
+## New in 0.7
+
+The indexed base-vertex fallback uses the driver directly when an index buffer
+is bound, GLES 3.2 or the base-vertex extension is supported, and the primitive
+restart mode needs no index rewrite. This avoids per-sub-draw GPU readback,
+CPU index widening and scratch-buffer uploads. Zero-base batches can use plain
+indexed drawing even without base-vertex support. Unsupported batches are rejected
+before any draw so fallback cannot draw an earlier sub-batch twice. This change
+helps calls reaching that fallback; existing native multidraw paths stay intact.
+
+Indirect command staging keeps its initialized high-water size instead of shrinking
+and then zero-filling memory that is overwritten by the next larger command batch.
+
+All 0.6 Quest and upload/presentation fixes remain. High chunk counts also increase
+world-generation, simulation, Java heap and GPU load. This renderer cannot guarantee
+zero lag with large modpacks; actual frame-time improvements need device measurements.
+
+## Earlier optimizations
 
 - Reuse initialized upload scratch storage without shrinking/re-zeroing between
   alternating small and large uploads. Existing large-buffer release policy stays.
